<title>SOUTH KOREA: Korea Green Cross '96 net rises.</title>
<headline>Korea Green Cross '96 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)				  2,490    vs 2,580</p>
<p>    Net						5.88 vs     5.51</p>
<p>    Turnover				     202.57 vs   173.65</p>
<p>Dividend in cash (pct, par 5,000 won)</p>
<p>	common shares				8    vs    12</p>
<p>	preferred shares			   9    vs    13</p>
<p>    Dividend in stocks (pct)		   3    vs    none</p>
<p>    Profit before tax			    8.23 vs     8.07</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		   0.12 (profit) vs 0.05 (loss)</p>
<p>NOTE - Korea Green Cross Corp is one of South Korea's leading pharmaceutical companies. It said earnings per share fell despite a rise in net profit due to increased number of shares issued. Its share capital rose to 2.49 million shares in 1996 from 2.25 million a year earlier.</p>
</text>
